{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788161285,"nonce":"SjsoYQrHRouGU4VVM87LWiDWgdo=","title":"ci: `ui-unit` and `ui-tests` are the same job — delete the duplicate","message":"`ui-unit` and `ui-tests` in `ci.yml` are the same job. Byte-identical: same\n`working-directory: ui/scarab-web-ui`, same `npm ci \u0026\u0026 npm test`, same\n`node-version: 22`, same cache path. Only the surrounding comments differ, and\nthey claim different tiers — `ui-unit` says \"test-strategy Phase 1 … the\nextracted derivation seam\", `ui-tests` says \"Phase 3 … the base of the UI\npyramid\". Both descriptions are of the one vitest suite that actually exists.\n\n`ci/ui-tests` is in `.github/required-checks.txt`; `ci/ui-unit` is not, so the\nduplicate is also the ungated one — it shows up in `just pr-gate` under \"not in\nrequired-checks.txt (ungated)\".\n\nFix: delete the `ui-unit` job. Keep `ui-tests`, which is the gated name. Fold\nwhichever half of the two comments is still true into the survivor.\n\nMeasured on PR #3: 0.3 min each, so this is about noise and honesty, not time —\ntwo green checks reporting one fact makes the check list read as more coverage\nthan exists.","files":null}]}